  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says that in the 1950s the United States had a craze for anti-gravity, the idea of craft that could cancel out gravity, and that by the 1960s it seemed to just vanish. Michels, who also points to the researcher Eric Weinstein, says the physicist Hal Puthoff told him that either the work went nowhere or it \"went black\", meaning it moved into secret, classified programmes. If it went black, the research would have kept going out of public view."
